---
source: crates/warden-schema/tests/parse_errors.rs
description: "definition doc {\n    permission view = (a1x - b1x) + c1x & folder.all(d1x)\n}"
---
error[E_AMBIGUOUS_OPERATORS]: `+` and `&` cannot be mixed without parentheses
 --> 2:41
  |
2 |     permission view = (a1x - b1x) + c1x & folder.all(d1x)
  |                                         ^
  |
  = note: SpiceDB gives `+` higher precedence than `&` and `-`, so it would read this as `((a1x - b1x) + c1x) & folder.all(d1x)`
  = help: add parentheses to say which grouping you mean, either
              ((a1x - b1x) + c1x) & folder.all(d1x)
          or
              (a1x - b1x) + (c1x & folder.all(d1x))
